WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:11.460
He’s a politician, but not just any politician.

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:15.930
His biography is what you’d expect from
the protagonist of a best selling political

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:16.930
fiction novel.

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:17.930
However...

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:22.440
my friends, this is a flesh and blood politician,
with both a good side and a dark side.

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:27.430
We’re talking about Benjamin Netanyahu,
Israel’s Prime Minister and the most powerful

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:47.210
politician the country has had in 

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:53.719
the last 2 decades.

00:00:53.719 --> 00:01:21.750
But... you may be wondering, why are we talking
about Netanyahu?

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.570
Why is he so important?

00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:28.039
Well, folks, what if I told you that this
man was the architect who basically designed

00:01:28.039 --> 00:01:29.940
the Israel we all know today?

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:31.140
Yes, you heard that right.

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:35.280
We’re talking about a politician who has
so much character that he actually attacked

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:38.800
the very president of the United States in
front of his own Congress.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:41.020
Yes, this happened to Barack Obama.

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:54.310
Don’t tell me 

00:01:54.310 --> 00:02:01.310
that isn’t one tough guy.

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:12.050
Well, the 

00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:19.810
fact is that Benjamin Netanyahu, or Bibi,
as he’s known in Israel, has done practically

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:21.700
everything in his country.

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:25.740
During his time as a soldier –remember,
military service is mandatory in Israel – he

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:31.311
commanded a special forces unit... and participated
in lots of operations like the ones we see

00:02:31.311 --> 00:02:33.530
in movies, with Hollywood-worthy names like:

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:38.071
Operation Inferno and operation Isotope, where,
by the way, Netanyahu was shot while he and

00:02:38.071 --> 00:02:47.880
his unit rescued a plane hijacked by the terrorist
group The Black September Organization

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:53.520
And as a soldier, he also participated in
operations in Egypt, Syria and Jordan.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:56.580
But... that’s not all.

00:02:56.580 --> 00:03:00.430
After finishing his military service, this
Prime Minister went to the United States to

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:01.430
study.

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:02.430
Where?

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:07.140
Well... in no other than, first, MIT, and
then Harvard.

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:08.850
By the way, here’s some curious trivia.

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:13.860
In 1973, when the Yom Kippur War broke out
between Israel and its Arab neighbors, Netanyahu,

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:18.490
who was studying in Boston, returned home
to re-join the special bodies forces until

00:03:18.490 --> 00:03:19.490
the war ended.

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:20.490
But... let's continue.

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:27.160
The fact is that after studying in the United
States and spending some time working in consulting,

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:29.460
he got involved in politics...

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:33.300
where, again, he’s done everything... he
has been a member of parliament, an Ambassador

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:38.260
to the UN, Minister of Foreign Affairs, Minister
of Finance and, of course, Prime Minister

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:39.400
for 4 terms.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:44.180
In fact, my friends, he’s about to become
the Israeli Prime Minister with the longest

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:45.530
term in office.

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:49.220
However, now his position of influence and
power is being questioned…

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:59.490
So, let's take a look at what’s happening
and why this man is an election-winning machine.

00:03:59.490 --> 00:04:05.830
(CORNERED)

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:11.209
On February 12th, 2018, after a year of investigations,
the Israeli police recommended the Attorney

00:04:11.209 --> 00:04:14.830
General bring charges against Benjamin Netanyahu.

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:20.989
See, the police state that there are clear
indications of corruption, bribes and influence

00:04:20.989 --> 00:04:21.989
peddling.

00:04:21.989 --> 00:04:26.200
They accuse the Prime Minister of having received
gifts of hundreds of thousands of dollars;

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:30.070
of having conspired to influence the media;
and also, of having protected millionaire

00:04:30.070 --> 00:04:34.260
corruption in the multimillion-dollar process
of buying German submarines.

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:38.430
And, you know what?

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:41.370
This isn’t the first time that the Israeli
Police accused him.

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:46.880
They also did it in 1997 and again in 1999,
during Netanyahu’s first term as Prime Minister.

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:52.430
Back then, the accusations ended with no charges...
and now again the Prime Minister has made

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:55.330
it very clear that he won’t yield.

00:04:55.330 --> 00:05:00.940
(“Nothing will have sway and nothing will
sway me, not even the incessant attacks against

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:01.940
me”.

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:02.940
Benjamin Netanyahu.)

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:07.530
The truth is that whether or not he’s finally
accused, Netanyahu is on the line.

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:10.020
By the way, in Israel, nobody is immune to
justice.

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:14.250
In the last decade they have condemned and
imprisoned a former prime minister, Ehud Olmert,

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:15.970
and an ex-president, Moshe Katzav.

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:19.970
So... if Netanyahu is guilty, he will pay.

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:24.910
Therefore, my friends, in this video we’ll
get to know Israel’s prime minister better,

00:05:24.910 --> 00:05:29.710
take a look at his good and bad sides and
investigate what made Netanyahu such an important

00:05:29.710 --> 00:05:35.700
character in Israel’s politics.

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:45.250
(KING BIBI: THE SAVIOR)

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:49.430
Netanyahu may not be the most amiable or popular
guy on the planet, but... one thing is certain...

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:54.060
Every time Bibi has come to power he’s done
so under very… very difficult conditions.

00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:59.840
See, during his first term, when he came to
power in 1996, the country was greatly unbalanced,

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:05.710
with an uncontrolled public deficit and a
growing external debt.

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:09.419
In 2003, when he was appointed Minister of
Finance under Ariel Sharon’s government,

00:06:09.419 --> 00:06:12.280
the country was undergoing its worst recession.

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:16.990
And the most current time was in 2009... just
when the country was suffering the consequences

00:06:16.990 --> 00:06:19.980
of the great international financial crisis.

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:24.030
Well... in all these cases Netanyahu's recipes
worked.

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:28.340
And not only that: with his policies, Bibi
has transformed this country’s identity.

00:06:28.340 --> 00:06:32.540
Thanks largely to his governance, Israel has
gone from being a place with chronic imbalances

00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:37.020
and crises, a country that in 1984 had to
be rescued by the United States...

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:42.550
to becoming a prosperous country, with well-organized
accounts and a worldwide power in technology

00:06:42.550 --> 00:06:49.310
and innovation...

00:06:49.310 --> 00:06:53.730
Through all this, we can understand how, despite
all the controversy, Bibi continues to raise

00:06:53.730 --> 00:06:57.480
passions, some against him, but many in favor
of him.

00:06:57.480 --> 00:06:59.860
But many of you may be thinking...

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:05.800
Okay, but what were or, rather, what are Benjamin
Netanyahu’s recipes?

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:09.830
Well, here they are.

00:07:09.830 --> 00:07:14.820
Traditionally, Israel was a socialist country,
with high taxes, a lot of regulation and a

00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:15.820
huge government.

00:07:15.820 --> 00:07:19.669
Well, Bibi’s mission was to change this
model once and for all and enforce another

00:07:19.669 --> 00:07:24.130
that would organize the accounts and improve
the country's competitiveness.

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:25.130
Check this out.

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:29.980
( “You think that mathematicians and computer
engineers or mechanical engineers or doctors

00:07:29.980 --> 00:07:30.980
are first.

00:07:30.980 --> 00:07:32.870
They’re very important, but they’re not
first.

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:33.919
They’re second.

00:07:33.919 --> 00:07:38.680
There was a country that had the best mathematicians,
the best physicists, the best metallurgists

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:39.680
in the world.

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:40.889
But that country was very poor.

00:07:40.889 --> 00:07:43.070
It’s called the Soviet Union.

00:07:43.070 --> 00:07:45.139
What comes first is markets.

00:07:45.139 --> 00:07:49.210
This was the main thing that I tried to bring
to the Israeli economy, in my own way”.

00:07:49.210 --> 00:07:50.500
Benjamin Netanyahu.)

00:07:50.500 --> 00:07:55.690
With this idea in mind, in his first mandate
in 1996, his number one priority was to reduce

00:07:55.690 --> 00:08:00.919
the public deficit, privatize banks and large
government-owned companies; and suppress capital

00:08:00.919 --> 00:08:01.919
controls.

00:08:01.919 --> 00:08:04.950
For example, at that time, Israelis had a
restriction on the money they could take out

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:07.630
of the country and for buying foreign currency.

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:11.539
Yes, we could say that the Israel of the early
90s resembled Cristina Fernández de Kirchner's

00:08:11.539 --> 00:08:15.070
Argentina: A lot of public spending and capital
controls.

00:08:15.070 --> 00:08:17.670
But... let's continue.

00:08:17.670 --> 00:08:24.800
In 2003, when the country was undergoing a
terrible crisis, as Minister of Finance...

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:29.410
a minister of finance with a lot of power,
Netanyahu froze public spending and launched

00:08:29.410 --> 00:08:31.139
a huge tax reduction.

00:08:31.139 --> 00:08:37.089
For example, he reduced corporate income tax,
as well as individual income tax, by half.

00:08:37.089 --> 00:08:43.339
See, when he arrived at the Ministry, the
maximum rate on income, in terms of wages,

00:08:43.339 --> 00:08:44.679
was 64%.

00:08:44.679 --> 00:08:46.260
When he left it was 44%.

00:08:46.260 --> 00:08:49.699
A 20 point reduction in 2 years!

00:08:49.699 --> 00:08:53.649
And when he came to power in 2009, he had
a similar recipe... less public spending,

00:08:53.649 --> 00:09:00.070
fewer taxes and less bureaucracy.

00:09:00.070 --> 00:09:03.889
In addition, in recent years, he managed to
get Israel, once and for all, to exploit its

00:09:03.889 --> 00:09:06.449
huge Natural Gas reserves.

00:09:06.449 --> 00:09:10.939
(“Israel bolsters Egypt ties with $15bn
gas deal”.

00:09:10.939 --> 00:09:11.939
Financial Times.)

00:09:11.939 --> 00:09:15.019
It was precisely because of this that many
believe Israel’s miracle would not have

00:09:15.019 --> 00:09:17.060
been possible without this Prime Minister.

00:09:17.060 --> 00:09:22.149
But don’t think that he only had good results
in the economic sector... not at all.

00:09:22.149 --> 00:09:28.029
( “In the 37 months that Netanyahu held
office, Israeli citizens enjoyed one of the

00:09:28.029 --> 00:09:32.129
safest and quietest periods with regards to
terrorism...

00:09:32.129 --> 00:09:38.399
Of the five Israeli leaders examined [Rabin,
Peres, Netanyahu, Barak, Sharon], Netanyahu’s

00:09:38.399 --> 00:09:42.560
policies with regards to the prevention and
deterrence of terrorism...were the most effective”.

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:43.560
Study by The Institute of Policy and Strategy,
The Lauder School and Interdisciplinary Center

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:44.560
Herzliya, 2002.)

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:48.220
Indeed, in addition to the economy, Israeli
society recognizes Netanyahu as having made

00:09:48.220 --> 00:09:50.370
Israel a safer country.

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:55.230
A safer country and also, very importantly,
a country that is much more open to the world...

00:09:55.230 --> 00:09:59.459
So much so that this Prime Minister has succeeded,
and listen up because I think this will amaze

00:09:59.459 --> 00:10:03.670
you, in getting relations between Israel and
the Arab countries to go…

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:04.670
well... smoothly.

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:09.610
Wait a second, Israel and the Arab countries?

00:10:09.610 --> 00:10:15.649
Let's look into this.

00:10:15.649 --> 00:10:18.660
(THE EXTERNAL APPROACH)

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:22.269
Do you know the popular saying?

00:10:22.269 --> 00:10:24.170
“My enemy’s enemy is my friend.”

00:10:24.170 --> 00:10:28.119
Well... it looks like something like this
is happening in the Middle East... with Iran

00:10:28.119 --> 00:10:31.480
and with fundamentalist groups like ISIS.

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:36.209
Check out the news that the New York Times
published on February 3rd, 2018.

00:10:36.209 --> 00:10:40.899
(“Secret Alliance: Israel Carries Out Airstrikes
in Egypt, With Cairo’s O.K”.

00:10:40.899 --> 00:10:41.899
New York Times.)

00:10:41.899 --> 00:10:45.639
Pay close attention to this news bomb.

00:10:45.639 --> 00:10:49.999
In the last 2 years, Israel has carried out
more than a hundred aerial attacks with planes,

00:10:49.999 --> 00:10:53.939
helicopters and drones against fundamentalist
groups in Egypt, particularly against the

00:10:53.939 --> 00:10:56.149
so-called Islamic State of Sinai.

00:10:56.149 --> 00:11:00.059
That is, an Arab government, in this case
the Egyptian government, has authorized Israel

00:11:00.059 --> 00:11:03.069
to carry out attacks and operations within
its territory.

00:11:03.069 --> 00:11:04.069
Amazing!

00:11:04.069 --> 00:11:05.420
But that’s not all.

00:11:05.420 --> 00:11:08.959
Israel's relations with Jordan and Egypt are
better than ever, but they’re also growing

00:11:08.959 --> 00:11:12.290
stronger with the other Arab countries, including
Saudi Arabia.

00:11:12.290 --> 00:11:13.649
Yes, you heard that right.

00:11:13.649 --> 00:11:17.139
Now, they still aren’t formal, but… they
are happening behind closed doors.

00:11:17.139 --> 00:11:21.529
(: “There is an alignment of Israel and
other countries in the Middle East that would

00:11:21.529 --> 00:11:24.589
have been unimaginable 10 years ago.

00:11:24.589 --> 00:11:28.800
Certainly in my life time, I never saw anything
like it and I'm at the age of the State of

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:31.600
Israel more or less, so it's an extraordinary
thing”.

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:32.600
Benjamin Netanyahu.)

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:33.600
Do you want another example?

00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:34.600
Well, listen up,

00:11:34.600 --> 00:11:37.399
After 70 years of prohibition, and for the
first time, Saudi Arabia has authorized an

00:11:37.399 --> 00:11:40.600
Israeli commercial flight to cross its airspace.

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:45.430
Since March, Air India flights between New
Delhi and Tel Aviv will cross Saudi airspace.

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:48.389
This may seem like a small step... but...
it’s not.

00:11:48.389 --> 00:11:49.389
And you know what?

00:11:49.389 --> 00:11:50.720
It’s not just the Arab countries.

00:11:50.720 --> 00:11:55.149
This Prime Minister has set his sights on
the East and has established surprisingly

00:11:55.149 --> 00:12:04.230
good relations with India, Australia, Singapore
and even China.

00:12:04.230 --> 00:12:19.850
What’s more, Netanyahu led the first visit
of an Israeli Prime Minister to Latin America.

00:12:19.850 --> 00:12:25.750
In 2017 he visited Mexico, Colombia and Argentina.

00:12:25.750 --> 00:12:39.649
And in Africa, more of the same.

00:12:39.649 --> 00:12:47.269
In fact, Netanyahu is the first Israeli leader
to visit this continent since the 1960s...

00:12:47.269 --> 00:12:52.069
and many African leaders are delighted with
Israel's money and technology.

00:12:52.069 --> 00:12:54.959
( “I saw diversity and richness.

00:12:54.959 --> 00:12:57.290
I saw passion and productivity.

00:12:57.290 --> 00:13:02.050
I saw young African entrepreneurs who are
building companies harnessing the power of

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:03.410
the digital age.

00:13:03.410 --> 00:13:05.279
Africans are seizing the future.

00:13:05.279 --> 00:13:07.600
Israel wants to seize this future with you.”

00:13:07.600 --> 00:13:08.600
Benjamin Netanyahu.)

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:12.459
In short, as you can see, both in the economic
field, as in security and foreign policy,

00:13:12.459 --> 00:13:14.980
this Prime Minister has many reasons to be
proud.

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:15.980
But of course…

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:21.829
not everything is a bed of roses.

00:13:21.829 --> 00:13:27.670
(THE DARK SIDE.)

00:13:27.670 --> 00:13:31.339
We’ve denounced it here on VisualPolik.

00:13:31.339 --> 00:13:35.449
One of Benjamin Netanyahu’s greatest dark
sides, in addition to his corruption suspicions,

00:13:35.449 --> 00:13:38.480
is his position towards the West Bank settlements.

00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:43.009
Yes, Netanyahu supports these settlements’
continual growth, and as we saw, in recent

00:13:43.009 --> 00:13:46.949
years his government has promoted a policy
to expand and consolidate them.

00:13:46.949 --> 00:13:52.149
( “In its more than three years in power,
this government has been irrational, bordering

00:13:52.149 --> 00:13:53.149
on messianic.

00:13:53.149 --> 00:13:58.720
It is now increasingly clear where it is headed:
creeping annexation of the West Bank aimed

00:13:58.720 --> 00:14:02.609
at precluding any permanent separation from
the Palestinians.”

00:14:02.609 --> 00:14:04.939
Ehud Barak, former Prime Minister of Israel.)

00:14:04.939 --> 00:14:09.769
And besides the settlements, Netanyahu’s
power relations with some magnates are also...

00:14:09.769 --> 00:14:11.329
how should I put it?

00:14:11.329 --> 00:14:12.329
Questionable.

00:14:12.329 --> 00:14:18.160
For example, his friend and gambling mogul,
Sheldon Adelson, invested $200 million in

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:22.899
the Israel Hayom, a free newspaper that greatly
favors Netanyahu.

00:14:22.899 --> 00:14:28.019
The question is, will he have to return these
favors?

00:14:28.019 --> 00:14:33.300
Another significant part of Netanyahu's dark
side has to do with his way of doing politics.

00:14:33.300 --> 00:14:38.829
Bibi is a tough opponent who has no qualms
about attacking his rivals through all possible

00:14:38.829 --> 00:14:39.829
means.

00:14:39.829 --> 00:14:44.449
That is precisely what he did in 1995 with
Prime Minister Yitzhak Rabin, whom he accused,

00:14:44.449 --> 00:14:47.279
among many other things, of betraying Jewish
values.

00:14:47.279 --> 00:14:51.329
The tension he generated was so great that
many detractors blame him for fueling the

00:14:51.329 --> 00:14:54.949
hatred that ended with Rabin's murder at the
hands of an extremist.

00:14:54.949 --> 00:14:58.829
His critics say that Netanyahu didn’t pull
the trigger, but that his lack of political

00:14:58.829 --> 00:15:01.319
piety led to the tragedy.

00:15:01.319 --> 00:15:07.519
So that, dear viewers, is the end of this
video about a politician who has a dark side…

00:15:07.519 --> 00:15:12.629
but also a significantly bright one as well,
contributing to make Israel a much more prosperous

00:15:12.629 --> 00:15:13.629
country.

00:15:13.629 --> 00:15:15.309
But now it’s your turn, what do you think
of Benjamin Netanyahu?

00:15:15.309 --> 00:15:18.570
Do you think King Bibi has been a good leader
for Israel?

00:15:18.570 --> 00:15:21.779
Leave your answer in the comments as well
as in the survey.

00:15:21.779 --> 00:15:25.389
I really hope you enjoyed this video, please
hit like if you did and don’t forget to

00:15:25.389 --> 00:15:28.189
subscribe to our channel for brand new videos
every Monday and Thursday.

